        "type": "Regex Injection",
        "severity": "high",
        "description": "Confirmed Regex Injection via DSBL_REJ option. The DSBL_REJ option value is retrieved from database/Option storage and used directly in preg_match() without validation. An attacker who can control this option value can inject malicious regex patterns leading to ReDoS or arbitrary code execution.",
        "recommendation": "Validate regex pattern before use with preg_match('/^.+$/s', $exc) or use a whitelist approach for URL exclusion.",
        "fix": "Before:\nif (preg_match($exc, $curPage)) {\n    return;\n}\n\nAfter:\n// Validate regex pattern first\nif (@preg_match($exc, '') === false) {\n    // Invalid pattern, skip\n    continue;\n}\nif (preg_match($exc, $curPage)) {\n    return;\n}",
        "reviewed": {
          "oldSeverity": "high",
